14 Jan 2020 18:16






Overall, the article is interesting and the writing is good.

But I fail to see why the Foundation would write an SCP about it. There is no evidence of any verifiable anomalous event related to the films, their content or people who watch them.

It's been created by an anartist, but not everything an anartist does has to be anomalous. He could very well have gone for 'regular' weird artist stuff. Sure, the disappearance of Dr Sinombre is intriguing but, in the given circumstances, we have no evidence that this event is of anomalous nature. And she is the only affected person.

My idea of SCP articles is very restrictive: I think it is primarily in-universe literature that compiles direct and indirect evidence of an anomalous phenomenon/object/entity. The Foundation would investigate the events of this article, of course, but there's not enough hard facts for it not to be eventually declassified.







